<title>AUSTRALIA: MOTOR CYCLING-SUPERBIKE WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>MOTOR CYCLING-SUPERBIKE WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results from the</p>
<p>opening round of the superbike world championship at Phillip</p>
<p>Island on Sunday:</p>
<p>First race:</p>
<p> 1. John Kocinski (U.S.) Honda 41 minutes 16.551 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Carl Fogarty (Britain) Ducati	   41:32.273</p>
<p> 3. Simon Crafar (New Zealand) Kawasaki   41:45.509</p>
<p> 4. Akira Yanagawa (Japan) Kawasaki	 41:57.457</p>
<p> 5. Troy Bayliss (Australia) Suzuki	 42:45.500</p>
<p> 6. Martin Craggill (Australia) Kawasaki  one lap behind</p>
<p> 7. Scott Russell (U.S.) Yamaha	     one lap</p>
<p> 8. Andy Meklau (Austria) Ducati	    one lap</p>
<p> 9. Shawn Giles (Australia) Honda	   one lap</p>
<p> 10. Pere Riba Cabana (Spain) Honda	 one lap</p>
<p>Second race</p>
<p> 1. Aaron Slight (New Zealand) Honda	35:33.916</p>
<p> 2. Colin Edwards (U.S.) Yamaha	     35:33.949</p>
<p> 3. Crafar					  35:34.673</p>
<p> 4. Fogarty					 35:42.145</p>
<p> 5. Bayliss					 35:51.923</p>
<p> 6. Russell					 35:56.570</p>
<p> 7. Kocinski					35:58.133</p>
<p> 8. Damon Buckmaster (Australia) Kawasaki 36:01.409</p>
<p> 9. Craggill					36:17.132</p>
<p> 10. Giles					  36:17.185</p>
<p>World championship standings after one round:</p>
<p> 1. Kocinski	  34 points</p>
<p> 2. Fogarty	   33</p>
<p> 3. Crafar	    32</p>
<p> 4. Slight	    25</p>
<p> 5. Bayliss	   22</p>
<p> 6. Edwards	   20</p>
<p> 7. Russell	   19</p>
<p> 8. Craggill	  17</p>
<p> 9. Yanagawa	  13</p>
<p>10. Buckmaster	 8</p>
<p>Next round: April 20 - Missano, San Marino</p>
</text>
